# HTML prototype frames — LOCKED

**Source of truth:** `design-reference/inbox-all-pages-html/prototype.html`  
**Screen → route map:** `design-reference/MAP.md`  
**Gap tracker:** `design-reference/GAPS.md`  
**Visual check:** `npm run check:html -- --screen <goId> --route <path>`

Canva PNG exports under `canva-reference/` are **archived**. Do not treat Canva
frames, old soft-radius comments, or `npm run check:canva` as binding for new UI.
When visual/IA conflicts with old Canva comments in Vue files, **follow the HTML
prototype as rendered in a browser**.

## Tokens (match the HTML)

- Crimson `#C41E1E`, charcoal `#2c2c2a`, mustard `#b68a3b`, silver `#8f8f8b`, off `#f4efe9`
- Green `#2e7d4f` / green-soft `#dcebe1`, mustard-soft `#f3e9d3`, line `rgba(44,44,42,.08)`
- Font: Vazirmatn (RTL body) — see persian-typography rule; do not swap stacks

## Visual rules (from the **rendered** prototype)

1. **Radius — SQUARE** — The HTML sets `*, *::before, *::after { border-radius: 0 !important }` (and the same on mobile shells `#m1`/`#m2`/`#m3`). **Do not** invent soft 10px buttons / 20px pills / 12–16px cards unless a specific HTML region visibly overrides it (rare). Prefer `border-radius: 0` / `--sz-canva-radius: 0`. Proto sticky nav pills in the HTML file are **prototype tooling only**, not product chrome.
2. **Icons** — HTML uses Tabler-style classes (`ti-bell`, `ti-calendar-event`, `ti-hand-stop`, …). Map chrome icons to the closest Material Symbols glyph **or** introduce Tabler for chrome. Never leave raw ligature text. Never use emoji as a permanent stand-in for HTML icons.
3. **No TailAdmin drift** — Do not invent soft dashboard chrome, purple gradients, or generic card grids that are not in the prototype.
4. **RTL align** — `text-start` / `justify-start` for right-aligned copy; never `text-end` for “align right”.
5. **Chrome** — Match the prototype shell for that role (public / athlete / coach / owner / admin) at the target breakpoint.
6. **Hero titles** — On photo heroes, force light/white titles when the prototype does (global navy `h1` is a bug).
7. **Search / primary CTAs** — Match the prototype’s searchbar and button hierarchy (labels, fields, crimson primary, calendar icon on date when HTML has it).
8. **No approximation** — List every region from the HTML screen; match sides, hierarchy, and IA. Use `design-reference/MAP.md` for `go()` → route. Update `GAPS.md`.
9. **Desktop + mobile** — The HTML includes both. Match the breakpoint the task targets; do not phone-only when the prototype shows a desk layout.
10. **Done gate** — Screenshot HTML (`go('…')`) vs live at the same width; attach pairs in chat / `design-reference/comparisons/`. Self-check before claiming done. `npm run check:html` is the visual gate; `check:canva` is historical only.
11. **Real photos** — Prototype stock photos are placeholders. Any hero tied to a club must use that club’s `image`, with `/hero/*` only as a `||` fallback.
12. **Product over mock** — Keep live APIs, auth, wallet, OTP, and escape-hatch chrome (bottom nav, back, logo). Do not paste the static HTML into production or strip navigation to “match a crop.” Mark intentional product extras as `kept-product` in `GAPS.md`.

## Explicit non-goals

- Do not revive Canva pixel overlays as the primary fidelity gate.
- Do not rename every `Canva*` Vue component in this foundation change — restyle/align screen-by-screen against the HTML.
- Digit/bidi/spacing: persian-typography rule still applies.
